  "summary_en": "Adds colour fringing that mimics lens behaviour, mainly near the frame edges, by separating and offsetting the red, green and blue channels. A Spectrum mode samples several wavelengths between the channel offsets for smoother fringing.",
  "inputs": [
    "source: the original layer",
    "effect (optional): per-pixel amount controlling the aberration strength",
    "mask (optional): per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Mode: RGB (offsets channels directly) or Spectrum (simulates wavelengths, converts back to RGB)",
    "Number of Colors: wavelength samples in Spectrum mode",
    "Pivot: centre for scale and rotation, default image centre",
    "Red / Green / Blue (distortion): per-channel scale offsets, defaults -0.15, 0, 0.15",
    "Global Distortion Scale: zoom-like scale for all channels, default 0.15, shaped by Distortion Scale Mask",
    "Red / Green / Blue (rotation) and Rotation Scale: rotation in degrees",
    "Red / Green / Blue (translation), Translation Scale and Translation Scale Mask",
    "Mask: blends the result with the original, 1 uses only the new result",
    "Filter: sampling method, default Box"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Spectrum mode and higher Number of Colors cost more to compute",
    "The page notes that a lens shader at render time is more physically accurate but renders slower"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Chromatic Aberration ajoute des franges de couleur près des bords de l'image en décalant séparément les canaux rouge, vert et bleu, avec un mode spectral plus doux en option."
